      "id": 22066,
      "name": "TheJayMann",
      "username": "TheJayMann",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-09-01T16:09:46.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I’ve found that having too many heroes out doesn’t give the villain a chance to do anything, even if you were to reset the play area.  Best way to do that would be to give the villain more turns per round.  (Think of it like, with so many heroes, they keep stepping on each others toes, or there’s only so much room, so they can’t move quite as fast as a single villain.)</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:56:07.718Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
